{"type":"npc","name":"Dedstre","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":140,"temp":0,"max":140,"details":""},"ac":{"value":24,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"cold","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"void","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["arboreal","cryan","fey"],"details":"can't speak any language"},"level":{"value":7},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Dedstres are withered tree husks that emerge from frozen woodlands, sapping the vitality of those who approach them. Despite their decrepit appearance and penchant for draining life energy, dedstres are not undead or even unnatural; they are merely an embodiment of winter's morbid role in the seasonal cycle. While they're sometimes confused with husks (Battlezoo Bestiary page 44) because of their appearance, dedstres consider husks their enemies; husks are unnatural blighted beings who live only to spread that blight and sow destruction, whereas dedstres might be morbid, but they're part of nature's cycle.</p><p>Dedstres thrive in freezing temperatures. When the cold months are prolonged, whether due to natural climate fluctuations or magical interference, they proliferate in greater numbers, spreading the cold further. Without the sun's warm touch and spring's verdant growth, frozen death can easily overrun the land. Though dedstres aren't typically hostile to other creatures, their incursions can present an existential threat to rural settlements. And once a dedstre has claimed an area, it is nearly impossible to convince them to move.</p><p>When spring at last returns in full force, most dedstres wither away, going dormant until the first nips of frost return.</p><h2>Dead of Winter</h2><p>A dedstre's chill goes beyond mere cold, and dedstres can sap the vitality of even the hardiest boreal forests. Dedstre migrations are frequently marked by paths of pine trees stripped bare of their needles. The destruction that dedstres wreak scatters local wildlife and makes them the enemies of some of the more friendly winter creatures, such as boreals and chionads. However, an area devastated by a dedstre is not totally without life: it makes a good breeding ground for crystalwing swarms.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 45/100/180 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), armor (medium, heavy), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Nature, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, death, energy resistant (cold, vitality), ice, sensory (low-light vision), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.IxhGEKl63R4QBvkj]{Frostbite}, @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.spells.FTjpdbJKibOcgZPN]{Winter's Grasp}), strength, tangle shield, throwing, wild, wisdom, wood</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Daniel Hutton","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":0},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"snow vision","mod":15,"senses":[{"type":"lifesense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60},{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":17,"special":[]},"nature":{"base":15,"special":[]},"survival":{"base":15,"special":[{"label":"to Track creatures in boreal forests","predicate":["action:track","terrain:forest","terrain:boreal"],"base":17}]}},"traits":{"value":["cold","plant"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"f8fvVzhvZW3O